# Guide: How to Get Your Google Service Account JSON

To verify subscriptions on your backend (app.py), your server needs a "Service Account" to talk to the Google Play API. Follow these steps to create one and get the JSON key.

---

## Step 1: Create a Service Account in Google Cloud

1.  Open the [Google Cloud Console](https://console.cloud.google.com/).
2.  Select the project associated with your app (or create a new one).
3.  In the left sidebar, go to **IAM & Admin** > **Service Accounts**.
4.  Click **+ CREATE SERVICE ACCOUNT** at the top.
5.  **Service account name**: Call it something like `hollowscan-iap-service`.
6.  Click **CREATE AND CONTINUE**.
7.  **Role**: You can leave this blank (Continue) as we will grant permissions in the Play Console instead.
8.  Click **DONE**.

---

## Step 2: Generate the JSON Key

1.  In the list of service accounts, click on the **Email** of the one you just created.
2.  Click on the **Keys** tab.
3.  Click **ADD KEY** > **Create new key**.
4.  Select **JSON** and click **CREATE**.
5.  A [.json](file:///c:/Users/Jo$h/Desktop/Visual%20Studio%20Code/HollowScan-Mobile-App/app.json) file will automatically download to your computer. **Keep this file safe!** 

---

## Step 3: Link the Service Account to Google Play Console

1.  Open your [Google Play Console](https://play.google.com/console/).
2.  In the left menu, scroll down to **Setup** > **API access**.
3.  (If you haven't linked a project yet, click **Link a project** and select the one from Step 1).
4.  Look for the **Service accounts** section at the bottom.
5.  Find the service account email you created and click **Grant access** (or "User permissions").
6.  In the **Account permissions** tab, ensure the following are checked:
    - [x] **View financial data, orders, and cancellation responses**
    - [x] **Manage orders and subscriptions**
7.  Click **Invite user** (or **Apply**).

---

## Step 4: Share the JSON with me

Once you have that [.json](file:///c:/Users/Jo$h/Desktop/Visual%20Studio%20Code/HollowScan-Mobile-App/app.json) file, you can copy its content and paste it here, or upload the file. I will use it to configure your backend to verify payments automatically.

> [!CAUTION]
> Never share this JSON file publicly (e.g., on GitHub). It grants full access to your Google Play subscription data.
